  "summary": "Confirmed three independent blank-screen vectors in both smartPollBoard (index.html:412) and smartPollFeatures (client.html:529): (1) Missing HTTP status checks — both functions call r.text() without verifying r.ok, so non-200 responses (error HTML) get parsed, find zero .stage-section elements, and trigger container.innerHTML replacement that blanks the board. Fix: change the first .then() to `return r.ok ? r.text() : Promise.reject()`. (2) Zero-sections guard missing — even valid 200 responses can transiently contain zero .stage-section elements, which triggers the `newSections.length !== curSections.length` branch and blanks the container. Fix: add `if (newSections.length === 0) return;` before the length comparison. (3) Cache poisoning — _lastBoardHTML/_lastFeaturesHTML is assigned before DOM diffing completes, so error or empty responses lock broken state into the cache and prevent recovery on the next poll. Fix: move cache assignment to after successful DOM update. All three fixes are needed in both polling functions (6 changes total)."
}
